Every SimpiCI job installs Dist::Zilla, this bundle and their requirements from scratch: ~219 CPAN modules, ~3 of the ~3.5 minutes per job. Measured on p5-app-codefork (run 39676019408, 2026-10-21): perl:5.40 job 3m26s = image pull 17s, cpanm Dist::Zilla ~1m50s, bundle + authordeps + listdeps ~1m15s, dzil test a few seconds. 12 Perl versions, 2 in parallel -> 22 minutes per push, for every dist on the provider.

Proposal:
- Build one image per supported Perl version, ghcr.io/getty/dzil-perl:<ver> (FROM perl:<ver>, cpanm Dist::Zilla + Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Author::GETTY + its authordeps + the usual author-test deps such as Test::Pod), published by a workflow in this repo: matrix over simpici-provider/perl-versions, on push to main, weekly schedule (fresh CPAN), workflow_dispatch.
- emit.sh writes the jobs as ghcr.io+getty+dzil-perl+<ver>+test.sh (SimpiCI maps that filename to ghcr.io/getty/dzil-perl:<ver>, job name stays unique per version). dzil-test.sh keeps "dzil authordeps --missing | cpanm" and "dzil listdeps --author --missing | cpanm" - they then only install what the image lacks (the dist own requirements, a newer bundle).
- Keep .simpici-apt working (the images are Debian-based perl images) and .simpici-perl / SIMPICI_PROVIDER_PERL_VERSIONS unchanged.
- The GitHub composite action dzil-test can use the same images as container.
- Check: the images must be public on ghcr so a consuming repo can pull them without credentials.
Expected: ~20-30s per job instead of ~3.5 min. Verify on a pure-perl consumer (p5-app-codefork) before/after.

